    skos:prefLabel "Fritjof Capra"@en ;
    rdfs:label "Fritjof Capra (human)"@en ;
    owl:sameAs <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fritjof_Capra> ;
    rdfs:comment "Austrian-born American physicist, systems theorist, and deep ecologist (b. February 1, 1939, Vienna). PhD, theoretical physics, University of Vienna (1966; doctoral advisor Walter Thirring); 20 years in particle-physics research at institutions including University of Paris, Lawrence Berkeley Laboratory, UC Santa Cruz, UC Berkeley, and San Francisco State University. Founding director (1995-2020), Center for Ecoliteracy, Berkeley; faculty, Amana-Key executive education program (São Paulo, Brazil); Fellow, Schumacher College (UK). Author of several real international bestsellers, including 'The Tao of Physics' (1975, still in print in 40+ editions), 'The Turning Point' (1982), 'The Web of Life' (1996), and 'The Hidden Connections' (2002); co-author with Pier Luigi Luisi of 'The Systems View of Life: A Unifying Vision' (Cambridge University Press, 2014)."@en ;
    .

